comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T21:28:05.779Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: fresh keyword searches and the complete all-status corpus found the completed original builder and warning-only MCP controls, but no owner for this newly filed report. Full live metadata/comments/history were read for the prior lineage. Preserve those closed outcomes and create only this distinct reported contract gap. Intake only: status open, unclaimed; no implementation or independent reproduction is claimed."
  "2026-10-21T22:33:53.878Z","harness:codex","Grouped with pm-gh1538 under one PR. Source inspection confirms ordinary generic command/manifest/profile builders and sibling literal widening. Plan compile-time failing-before controls, contextual callback checks, supported customization compatibility, and packed public entrypoint verification before closure."
  "2026-10-21T22:40:56.257Z","harness:codex","Regression evidence: public aggregate/authoring compile fixture fails on baseline with widened command name/action/examples and sibling builder literals, unused expected-error directives for command/manifest/profile typos, and rejection of supported repeatable/value_validation flag metadata. Const generic exact-key builders now pass the same compile fixture with contextual callbacks. Existing reference-identity tests pass; no runtime validation or private consumer imports were introduced."
  "2026-10-21T22:49:35.117Z","harness:codex","Public SDK snapshot regenerated from emitted declarations, recording22 signature changes across aggregate and authoring entrypoints with an explicit source-compatibility acknowledgement for documented exact keys and const literal inference. All object/scoped-object builder definitions retain zero-cost identity, and supported repeatable/value_validation flag metadata now reaches authoring without a cast. Package doctor reports clean activation and latest available pm-changelog installation succeeds. Public docs describe widened pre-existing variables and keeping package annotations outside registration objects."
  "2026-10-22T01:06:46.338Z","harness:codex","Final verification: the packed public SDK passes strict TypeScript 5.9.3 declarations, deliberately degraded literal/exactness control, restored declarations, and Node/Bun activation and runtime identity. Maintained packed npm/npx/Bun/bunx smoke passes. All linked tests pass and the complete repository coverage run passes with 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines. No coverage denominator, timeout, assertion or quality threshold was reduced. Source-level static checks, import costs and transport floors passed; the graph gate identified new prose references and was repaired through explicit related edges instead of a limit change. The final full static pipeline, terminal defect evidence and generated changelog are required before push."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T23:08:11.664Z","harness:codex","An ordinary constrained generic does not enforce excess properties or preserve string literals. Object authoring builders need const type parameters and exact-key constraints; function callbacks should retain contextual typing, and compile fixtures must use the public aggregate and narrow entrypoints. Audit supported flag keys against the registration interface when tightening builders."
